  "raw_label": "appellant_lost",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Vijay Babasaheb Lembhe vs The Commissioner Of Police And Another on 21 June, 2024 2024:Bhc-Aug:11622 In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Bench At Aurangabad Anticipatory Bail Application No. 772 Of 2024 Harshal S/O Vijaykumar Patil Versus The Commissioner Of Police And Another Mr. Mohd. Aseem Mohd. A. K., Advocate for the applicant Mrs. K. R. Jamdhade, App for the respondent/State And Anticipatory Bail Application No. 733 Of 2024 Vijay Babasaheb Lambhe Versus The Commissioner Of Police And Another Mr. A. R. Borulkar, Advocate for the applicant Mrs. K. R. Jamdhade, App for the respondent/State Coram : R. M. Joshi, J. Date : 21st June, 2024 Per Court :- 1. Applicant apprehends arrest in connection with Crime No. 25/2024 registered with Jinsi Police Station, Dist. Aurangabad for the offences punishable under Sections 328, 273, 188 of IPC, 26(1), 26(2) (iv), 27(3)(d), 27(3)(e), 30(2)(a), 59 of Food Safety and Standard Act and 7(2) of the Cigarette and other Tobacco Products (Prohibition on Advertisement and Regulation of Trade and Commerce, Production, Supply and Distribution) Act. 904.aba772.24.odt 1 of 2 Vijay Babasaheb Lembhe vs The Commissioner Of Police And Another on 21 June, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/8167077/",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "1 2. It is the contention of the learned counsel for the applicants that the name of the applicants does not appear in the first information report to be the persons from whose custody the contraband articles are seized. 3. Learned APP opposed the application by contending that during the course of the investigation name of the applicants have revealed as supplier of the contraband articles and hence, they are not entitled for anticipatory bail. Learned APP informed the Court that the present applicants are found involved in similar crime earlier and they are enlarged on bail."
  },
